    "user_title": "Build Azure Event Hubs Workflows in TypeScript",
    "value_statement": "Building reliable Event Hubs producers and consumers requires correct authentication, batching, partitioning, and checkpoint management. This skill provides focused TypeScript patterns for those tasks.",
    "seo_keywords": [
      "Azure Event Hubs",
      "TypeScript event streaming",
      "Azure SDK",
      "EventHubProducerClient",
      "EventHubConsumerClient",
      "Blob checkpoint store",
      "Claude",
      "Codex",
      "Claude Code"
    ],
    "actual_capabilities": [
      "Shows package installation and DefaultAzureCredential authentication for Azure Event Hubs.",
      "Demonstrates batched event production with partition identifiers and partition keys.",
      "Builds consumer subscriptions with event and error handlers.",
      "Configures Azure Blob Storage checkpointing for consumer groups.",
      "Selects consumer start positions by offset, timestamp, or stream boundary.",
      "Explains event properties, batch controls, hub metadata, and client cleanup."
    ],
    "limitations": [
      "Provides reference examples, not a complete runnable application or deployment.",
      "Requires existing Azure resources, permissions, dependencies, and environment configuration.",
      "Does not provision infrastructure or define detailed RBAC, networking, monitoring, and retention policies.",
      "Checkpointing does not guarantee exactly-once side effects; consumers still need idempotency or deduplication."
    ],
    "use_cases": [
      {
